
MILPE demo #105 - Data-driven Riemann Zeta Function

s = 0.5 + i*t;
z = zeta(s);
x = real(z);
y = imag(z);

Consider RZF trajectory as function of t (where t stands for imaginary part in euler space)
and get derivative of x and y respect to t.

% 1st derivatives
for i=2:m
    u(i) = (x(i)-x(i-1))/dt;
    v(i) = (y(i)-y(i-1))/dt;
end
u(1) = u(2);
v(1) = v(2);

% 2nd derivatives
for i=2:m
    udot(i) = (u(i)-u(i-1))/dt;
    vdot(i) = (v(i)-v(i-1))/dt;
end
udot(1) = udot(2);
vdot(1) = vdot(2);

Then find the approx dynamic system that uses inputs u, v and their H.O.T and outputs udot, vdot.

Current status
- extracting eigenvectors and thus approx GE seems to stable when shorter amount of RZF data is used (but never knows)
- Current Bases are [u v uv uuv uvv uuu vvv] for both udot and vdot.
- need to find correct Hilbert space. Lacking module.
- also need to consider how sensitive to dt (delta t). currently using 1e-4 and 1e-5 and testing 1e-6 -> 1e-5 seems okay
- 0<t<12 seems transitional, so better truncate
